{"resourceIdentifier":"2964","resourceName":"POLATLI ENERBES BIOGAS PROJECT","description":"Polatlı Enerbes Biogas Project is a biogas to-energy project that will generate renewable energy by capturing biogas from animal manure -via anaerobic digestion- and utilizing it to produce thermal and electric energy through biogas systems. The project is being implemented  in Çanakçı village, Polatlı district, Ankara province, in Turkey. The project whose main feedstock will be cattle and chicken manure generated at farms in Polatlı, provides an environmentally friendly solution to this manure management problem. it is estimated that approximately 1,178 tons of cattle manure and 22 tons of chicken manure (totally 1,200 tons) generated at nearby animal farms will be collected daily through special sewage trucks equipped with close-tanks in order to prevent any odor and/or manure leakages and to be fed into the anaerobic digesters at the biogas power plant. The biogas that will be released during the biodegradation of organic wastes will be used for electricity and heat production in biogas unit. The proposed project activity has 3 biogas engines installed at the biogas power plant, with the total capacity of 4,500 KWe/h. Accordingly, the biogas generator system to be installed will be designed with a total power of 4.50 MWe/h. Whilst heat generated at the plant is used at the facility to warm the digesters, the electricity generated is directly fed to the national grid. This project adopts the renewable crediting period of 7 years, twice renewable for a total of 21 years. The expected average annual emission reductions are 529,993 tCO2eq/y. Accordingly, the project is expected to generate 3,709,951 tCO2eq emissions reduction during the first crediting period.","location":{"latitude":39.472017,"longitude":32.071179},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-04-18","endExclusive":"2022-05-19","endInclusive":"2022-05-18"},"attributes":[{"co